    <div id="opane-about" class="opane" hidden>
      <h3>About this companion</h3>
      <div class="callout callout-pastoral">
        <p>This companion reflects the fasting designations published by the Greek Orthodox Archdiocese of America. Individual fasting practices may be adjusted with the guidance of one's parish priest or spiritual father, particularly for children, pregnancy, illness, medication, demanding work, travel, eating disorders, or other pastoral and medical needs.</p>
        <p>Fasting is not merely a dietary program; it belongs within prayer, repentance, worship, almsgiving, and life in Christ.</p>
      </div>
      <h4>Sources</h4>
      <ul class="sources">
        <li><a href="https://www.goarch.org/chapel/planner" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOARCH Planner: Ecclesiastical Digital Calendar</a> — the controlling source. Every fasting designation, saint and reading citation in this app is parsed directly from the official Planner ICS for 2025&ndash;2026.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.goarch.org/chapel/calendar" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOARCH Online Chapel calendar</a> — the same data on the web, and where the full reading text can be read.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.goarch.org/transfiguration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOARCH — Transfiguration of our Lord</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.goarch.org/dormition" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOARCH — Dormition of the Theotokos</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.goarch.org/-/the-calendar-of-the-orthodox-church" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GOARCH — The Calendar of the Orthodox Church</a>, which gives the Dormition fast as August 1 to 14.</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>What this app does not contain</h4>
      <p>No patristic quotations, sayings of saints, hymn texts or liturgical texts are reproduced here. The reflection prompts are ordinary questions written for this app, not quotations from anyone. Where something belongs to Tradition rather than to Scripture, the text says so.</p>
      <h4>Images</h4>
      <p>Every graphic shipped with this app is an original SVG drawn in code — the three-bar cross, the borders, the ornaments, the app icon. No feast icon is bundled. Instead the Feasts screen lets you add your own properly licensed image, which is stored on this device along with the credit and licence you record. The README names two public-domain files that fit.</p>
      <p class="small" id="verify-note"></p>
